{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782088253815,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4469b6919ad4478db6707ed9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/brazilian-soccer-mcp-guide.md","limit":50},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/brazilian-soccer-mcp-guide.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: This document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## Purpose\n10: \n11: - **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n12: - **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n13: - **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## Provided Data\n18: \n19: The following datasets are included in `data/kaggle/` and must be used:\n20: \n21: ### Match Data\n22: \n23: #### 1. Brasileirão Serie A Matches\n24: **File**: `Brasileirao_Matches.csv` (4,180 matches)\n25: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n26: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n27: \n28: | Column | Description |\n29: |--------|-------------|\n30: | datetime | Match date and time |\n31: | home_team | Home team name with state suffix (e.g., \"Palmeiras-SP\") |\n32: | home_team_state | State abbreviation |\n33: | away_team | Away team name with state suffix |\n34: | away_team_state | State abbreviation |\n35: | home_goal | Goals scored by home team |\n36: | away_goal | Goals scored by away team |\n37: | season | Year of the season |\n38: | round | Match round number |\n39: \n40: #### 2. Copa do Brasil Matches\n41: **File**: `Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv` (1,337 matches)\n42: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n43: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n44: \n45: | Column | Description |\n46: |--------|-------------|\n47: | round | Cup round |\n48: | datetime | Match date and time |\n49: | home_team | Home team name |\n50: | away_team | Away team name |\n\n(Showing lines 1-50 of 390. Use offset=51 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\n- **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n- **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n- **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n\n---\n\n## Provided Data\n\nThe following datasets are included in `data/kaggle/` and must be used:\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/brazilian-soccer-mcp-guide.md","text":"# Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\n- **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n- **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n- **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n\n---\n\n## Provided Data\n\nThe following datasets are included in `data/kaggle/` and must be used:\n\n### Match Data\n\n#### 1. Brasileirão Serie A Matches\n**File**: `Brasileirao_Matches.csv` (4,180 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| datetime | Match date and time |\n| home_team | Home team name with state suffix (e.g., \"Palmeiras-SP\") |\n| home_team_state | State abbreviation |\n| away_team | Away team name with state suffix |\n| away_team_state | State abbreviation |\n| home_goal | Goals scored by home team |\n| away_goal | Goals scored by away team |\n| season | Year of the season |\n| round | Match round number |\n\n#### 2. Copa do Brasil Matches\n**File**: `Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv` (1,337 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| round | Cup round |\n| datetime | Match date and time |\n| home_team | Home team name |\n| away_team | Away team name |","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":50,"totalLines":390,"truncated":true}},"title":"brazilian-soccer-mcp-guide.md","time":{"start":1782088253809,"end":1782088253814}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_eecbcbe90001u90GXS7NdY8LSH","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecbcb968001VLfkgUUYDSMmke"}}
