ontent":"Implement Core: models, CSV loader, team-name normalization, date parsing, query service","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement MCP Server with tools wrapping the query service","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write BDD (LightBDD) tests covering match/team/player/competition/stat queries","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Build all projects and run tests; fix failures","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update README.md with what was implemented","status":"pending","priority":"medium"}],"truncated":false},"title":"6 todos","time":{"start":1782088289157,"end":1782088289159}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"LightBDD.XUnit2 v3.12.0 is available. I'll use it for BDD-style tests. \n\nNow let me plan the implementation. I'll set up a todo list.\n\nProject structure:\n```\nBrazilianSoccerMcp.sln\nsrc/\n  BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/     (class library, net10.0)\n  BrazilianSoccerMcp.Server/   (console app, MCP server, net10.0)\ntests/\n  BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/    (xunit + LightBDD, net10.0)\n```\n\nLet me check what the ModelContextProtocol 1.4.0 package exposes for tools. I recall the API. Let me check via nuget metadata or just rely on docs. I'll write the code based on the documented pattern.\n\nActually let me look at the modelcontextprotocol GitHub repo to confirm the API. The package is at https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/csharp-sdk. Version 1.4.0 corresponds to current state. The API:\n\n- `Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting` based\n- `builder.Services.AddMcpServer().WithStdioServerTransport().WithToolsFromAssembly();`\n- Tool attribute: `[McpServerTool]` in `ModelContextProtocol.Server`\n- Tool type attribute: `[McpServerToolType]`\n- Methods return string or JsonElement or AOT-serialized types\n\nLet me just proceed. I'll write the code.\n\nLet me create a todo list and start.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecbd43ce001aYSc49