{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782088559643,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8560307d519bf46a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"// BrazilianSoccerMcp.Server - MCP server entry point.\n// Hosts the tools from this assembly over the stdio MCP transport so an MCP\n// client (e.g. Claude Desktop, an LLM agent) can invoke them. Logging is\n// redirected to stderr to keep stdout reserved for the JSON-RPC protocol.\nusing BrazilianSoccerMcp.Server.Tools;\nusing Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting;\nusing Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;\nusing ModelContextProtocol.Server;\n\nvar builder = Host.CreateApplicationBuilder(args);\n\n// MCP speaks JSON-RPC over stdout, so force all framework logs to stderr.\nbuilder.Logging.AddFilter(\"Microsoft\", LogLevel.Warning);\nbuilder.Logging.AddFilter(\"System\", LogLevel.Warning);\nbuilder.Logging.AddSimpleConsole(o => o.LogToStandardErrorThreshold = LogLevel.Trace);\n\nbuilder.Services\n    .AddMcpServer()\n    .WithStdioServerTransport()\n    .WithToolsFromAssembly();\n\nawait builder.Build().RunAsync();\n","filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Server/Program.cs"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Server/Program.cs","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Server/Program.cs","time":{"start":1782088559640,"end":1782088559642}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The `DataContext` class is internal and has a `Query` property that returns `SoccerQueryService`. But I access `DataContext.Query.FindMatchesByTeam(...)` from the tool classes. `DataContext` is `internal static class` in the same namespace `BrazilianSoccerMcp.Server.Tools` — yes, it's declared in that file in that namespace. Good.\n\nNow write Program.cs for the MCP host.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecc160d0001PBIdP0MU0e2xOI","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecc157ee001elK1PI41bTaNOW"}}
