\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tBotafogo-RJ\tRJ\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tCeara-CE\tCE\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tChapecoense-SC\tSC\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tCorinthians-SP\tSP\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tCruzeiro-MG\tMG\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tCsa-AL\tAL\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tFlamengo-RJ\tRJ\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tFluminense-RJ\tRJ\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tFortaleza-CE\tCE\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tGoias-GO\tGO\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tGremio-RS\tRS\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tInternacional-RS\tRS\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tPalmeiras-SP\tSP\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tSantos-SP\tSP\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tSao Paulo-SP\tSP\nAtletico-MG\tMG\tVasco da Gama-RJ\tRJ\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tAtletico-MG\tMG\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tAvai-SC\tSC\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tBahia-BA\tBA\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tBotafogo-RJ\tRJ\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tCeara-CE\tCE\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tChapecoense-SC\tSC\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tCorinthians-SP\tSP\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tCruzeiro-MG\tMG\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tCsa-AL\tAL\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tFlamengo-RJ\tRJ\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tFluminense-RJ\tRJ\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tFortaleza-CE\tCE\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tGoias-GO\tGO\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tGremio-RS\tRS\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tInternacional-RS\tRS\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tPalmeiras-SP\tSP\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tSantos-SP\tSP\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tSao Paulo-SP\tSP\nAtletico-PR\tPR\tVasco da Gama-RJ\tRJ\nAvai-SC\tSC\tAtletico-MG\tMG\nAvai-SC\tSC\tAtletico-PR\tPR\n","exit":0,"description":"List unique 2019 Brasileirao teams","truncated":false},"title":"List unique 2019 Brasileirao teams","time":{"start":1782088658161,"end":1782088658163}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The MCP server works end-to-end. The standings calculation shows \"Atletico\" with 112 points as champion for 2019 — that's wrong; Flamengo won 2019 with 90 points. The issue is that \"Atletico\" is matching multiple distinct teams (Atlético-MG, Athletico-PR, Atlético-GO) because my normalizer strips the state suffix and they all become \"Atletico\". So all their matches get aggregated into one \"Atletico\" team.\n\nThis is a real data quality problem. The historical file uses \"Athletico-PR\" and the Brasileirão file uses \"Athletico-PR\" too perhaps, or \"Atletico-MG\". When I strip \"-PR\"/\"-MG\", they all collapse to \"Atletico\"/\"Athletico\". Note \"Athletico\" vs \"Atletico\" — different spelling, but after diacritic stripping and lowercasing, \"athletico\" != \"atletico\". Hmm. But the aggregation shows \"Atletico\" with 112 pts which suggests multiple Atlético teams merged.\n\nActually for the 2019 Brasileirão (Brasileirao_Matches.csv), the teams are \"Atletico-MG\", \"Athletico-PR\" etc.? Let me check. The spec said home_team has state suffix. So \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Athletico-PR\" would normalize to keys \"atletico\" and \"athletico\" respectively — different. So why 112 points?\n\nWait, maybe there's also \"Atletico-GO\" in 2019? Atlético Goianiense was in Serie A 2019? Actually they were promoted in 2019 maybe. \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-GO\" both normalize to \"atletico\" → merged. That would inflate.\n\nThis is a genuine normalization challenge: stripping the state suffix loses disambiguation for teams that share a base name. The spec explicitly mentions team name variations and says \"normalize team names for consistent matching\" — but over-normalization merges distinct clubs.\n\nThe real Flamengo 2019 had 90 pts and won. My result has Flamengo at 90 in 2nd but \"Atletico\" at 112 in 1st. The 112 is clearly two Atléticos merged (Atletico-MG + Atletico-GO). \n\nHow to fix? I should NOT strip the state suffix when it's needed for disambiguation. Better approach: keep the state suffix as part of the canonical key, OR only strip the suffix if there's no collision. The cleanest correct approach: use the base name + state as the team identity, but allow matching by display name without suffix when unambiguous.\n\nActually, a common real-world approach: the canonical team identity should retain the state code. So \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-GO\" are different teams. But then a user query \"Atletico\" would be ambiguous. For the standings calculation, we want distinct teams.\n\nLet me reconsider the normalizer. The key should be the base name WITHOUT stripping the state, but normalized (diacritics stripped, lowercased, spacing trimmed). Wait but then \"Palmeiras-SP\" and \"Palmeiras\" (from a file without suffix) would be different keys. That breaks cross-file matching for the majority of teams.\n\nBetter hybrid: \n- Compute a \"display core\" (strip state) for display.\n- Compute the canonical key as base_name + \"|\" + state. If state is empty, key is just base_name.\n- For matching, when querying by a user-supplied name that has no state, match all teams whose base_name matches (could be multiple). When the base_name uniquely maps to one team, use it; otherwise it's ambiguous.\n\nThat's more complex. For standings, we group by the full identity (base+state). So \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-GO\" become separate rows. For team queries by \"Atletico\", we'd return matches from both — ambiguous but acceptable, or we could require disambiguation.\n\nFor a benchmark/demo, the cleanest fix that keeps cross-file matching working AND avoids merging distinct clubs: include the state in the key. So:\n- Key = normalized(base_name) + \"::\" + normalized(state)\n- For files without state (Copa do Brasil, Libertadores, BR-Football), state is unknown — key = normalized(base_name) + \"::\" (empty state). \n\nBut that would split Palmeiras across files: \"palmeiras::sp\" (Brasileirao) vs \"palmeiras::\" (Libertadores). That breaks cross-file.\n\nHmm. This is genuinely hard. Let me look at the actual data to see how teams appear across files. Let me check what team names appear in Libertadores and Copa do Brasil for Brazilian teams — do they have state suffixes?\n\nFrom the sample: Libertadores has \"Barcelona-EQU\", \"Boca Juniors\", \"Nacional (URU)\". Copa do Brasil has \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\", \"América - MG\". So Copa do Brasil has state suffixes (with spaced dash). Libertadores has some suffixes for non-Brazilian teams but Brazilian teams? Let me check.\n\nThe real issue is only for teams that share a base name across states lines: Atletico (MG, PR, GO), America (MG, RN, etc.), Botafogo (RJ, SP, PB...), Sport, etc. \n\nGiven this is a demo, the pragmatic solution: keep the state in the canonical key, but ALSO build an alias map so that a bare base name resolves correctly when unambiguous. For standings, group by full key. For team queries, if the user's query has a state, use full key; if not, match by base name and if multiple distinct full-keys exist, either aggregate (current behavior, which is wrong for standings) or pick... \n\nActually, for standings we MUST group by distinct team identity. So group by full key (base+state). That fixes the 2019 champion issue: Atletico-MG and Atletico-GO become separate.\n\nFor team stat queries \"GetTeamStats('Atletico')\", aggregating both Atléticos is arguably acceptable (it's what the user asked — ambiguous). But better to resolve to the most prominent one or require state. For the benchmark, let me keep it simple: team queries match by base name and aggregate all matching full-identities (so \"Atletico\" stats include all Atléticos). That's a known limitation but documented. For standings, group by full identity so the table is correct.\n\nLet me restructure the normalizer and the service:\n- `TeamNameNormalizer` produces:\n  - `BaseName(raw)` — display name without state, diacritics kept\n  - `BaseKey(raw)` — normalized base (lowercase, no diacritics)\n  - `StateCode(raw)` — the state suffix or \"\"\n  - `FullKey(raw)` — baseKey + \"|\" + state (state lowercased)\n- In the service, index by fullKey. Build a `baseKey -> list<fullKey>` map for resolving ambiguous bare queries.\n- `ResolveTeam(teamName)`: if user provided a state, use fullKey; else if baseKey maps to exactly one fullKey, use it; else return the base display name (and queries aggregate all).\n- `FindMatchesByTeam`: match by baseKey (aggregates all teams sharing base name) — this matches user expectation for \"all Palmeiras matches\" and is fine. Actually for correctness maybe better: if user gave state, filter to that fullKey; else match all fullKeys with that baseKey.\n- Standings: group by fullKey, display name = baseName + \"-\" + state (or just baseName if no state). \n\nHmm but then standings rows for \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-GO\" would both show. Display should include state to distinguish. Let me make display for standings = baseName + (state ? \"-\"+state : \"\").\n\nWait, but the Brasileirão file already has state for every team, so every row will have a state. Good. Historical file also has state (Mandante_UF). Copa do Brasil has state in the team name (spaced dash) — my parser extracts it. Libertadores may not have state for Brazilian teams. BR-Football has no state at all.\n\nFor standings I'm computing per-competition per-season. For Brasileirão 2019, all teams come from Brasileirao_Matches.csv which has state. So grouping by fullKey works and disambiguates Atletico-MG vs Atletico-GO. \n\nLet me implement this. I'll refactor TeamNameNormalizer to expose BaseName, BaseKey, StateCode, FullKey. Update SoccerQueryService to use FullKey for indexing and standings grouping, and BaseKey for bare-name team queries.\n\nAlso display name in standings should include state. Let me make the ResolveTeam for standings context include state.\n\nLet me rewrite the normalizer and adjust the service. This is important for correctness (the 2019 champion should be Flamengo).\n\nLet me check the actual team names in Brasileirao 2019 to confirm Atletico-MG/GO and the states.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecc2e54c001L7dFrbd2CWEkii","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecc27164001Nak5P8vr6SfuVq"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1782088658238,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"id":"prt_eecc2ed3d001cwbF0068mDqh4I","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"13165ce4f2948ebb9acd8e7ceab3340d10167213","messageID":"msg_eecc27164001Nak5P8vr6SfuVq","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":60729,"input":705,"output":120,"reasoning":2070,"cache":{"write":0,"read":57834}},"cost":0.0213918}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1782088659217,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"id":"prt_eecc2f109001Xod26QzYLbhS7J","messageID":"msg_eecc2ed8d001XKeUznszDMC5x4","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","snapshot":"13165ce4f2948ebb9acd8e7ceab3340d10167213","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782088673172,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ab7f071888acda6a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"// BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core - Team name normalization.\n// The five match CSV files use a mix of naming conventions for the same team:\n//   * \"Palmeiras-SP\"        (state suffix after a dash, no spaces)\n//   * \"Palmeiras - SP\"      (state suffix after a spaced dash)\n//   * \"Palmeiras\"           (no suffix)\n//   * \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" (full legal name)\n//   * \"América - MG\"        (accented, spaced dash)\n// Two distinct clubs can share a base name across states (e.g. \"Atletico-MG\"\n// and \"Atletico-PR\"), so the canonical identity RETAINS the state code. The\n// base name (suffix stripped, accents preserved) is used for display and for\n// bare-name queries that should match every club with that base name.\nusing System.Globalization;\nusing System.Text;\n\nnamespace BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core.Data;\n\n/// <summary>\n/// Produces canonical team-name keys and human-friendly display names that\n//  keep distinct same-base clubs (e.g. Atletico-MG vs Atletico-PR) separate.\n/// </summary>\npublic static class TeamNameNormalizer\n{\n    // Brazilian state abbreviations used as suffixes in the source data.\n    private static readonly HashSet<string> States = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)\n    {\n        \"AC\",\"AL\",\"AP\",\"AM\",\"BA\",\"CE\",\"DF\",\"ES\",\"GO\",\"MA\",\"MT\",\"MS\",\"MG\",\n        \"PA\",\"PB\",\"PR\",\"PE\",\"PI\",\"RJ\",\"RN\",\"RS\",\"RO\",\"RR\",\"SC\",\"SP\",\"SE\",\"TO\"\n    };\n\n    /// <summary>Base name with the state suffix removed but accents/case kept.</summary>\n    public static string BaseName(string raw)\n    {\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(raw)) return \"\";\n        var trimmed = raw.Trim();\n        var (core, _) = SplitState(trimmed);\n        return core.Trim();\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Two-letter state code extracted from the suffix, or \"\" if none.</summary>\n    public static string StateCode(string raw)\n    {\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(raw)) return \"\";\n        var (_, state) = SplitState(raw.Trim());\n        return state ?? \"\";\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Display name: base name, plus \"-UF\" when a state is present.</summary>\n    public static string DisplayName(string raw)\n    {\n        var baseName = BaseName(raw);\n        var state = StateCode(raw);\n        return state.Length > 0 ? $\"{baseName}-{state}\" : baseName;\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Normalized base-name key (accent-stripped, lowercased).</summary>\n    public static string BaseKey(string raw) =>\n        RemoveDiacritics(BaseName(raw)).ToLowerInvariant().Trim();\n\n    /// <summary>Full canonical identity key: baseKey + \"|\" + state(lower).</summary>\n    public static string FullKey(string raw)\n    {\n        var baseKey = BaseKey(raw);\n        var state = StateCode(raw).ToLowerInvariant();\n        return $\"{baseKey}|{state}\";\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Strips diacritics so \"São Paulo\" matches \"Sao Paulo\".</summary>\n    public static string RemoveDiacritics(string text)\n    {\n        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(text)) return text;\n        var sb = new StringBuilder();\n        foreach (var c in text.Normalize(NormalizationForm.FormD))\n        {\n            var category = char.GetUnicodeCategory(c);\n            if (category != UnicodeCategory.NonSpacingMark &&\n                category != UnicodeCategory.SpacingCombiningMark)\n            {\n                sb.Append(c);\n            }\n        }\n        return sb.ToString().Normalize(NormalizationForm.FormC);\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Splits a raw team name into (baseName, stateCode?) by the last dash.</summary>\n    private static (string Core, string? State) SplitState(string value)\n    {\n        var dashIndex = value.LastIndexOf('-');\n        while (dashIndex >= 0)\n        {\n            var tail = value.Substring(dashIndex + 1).Trim();\n            // \"Palmeiras-SP\"        -> tail = \"SP\"\n            // \"América - MG\"        -> tail = \"MG\"\n            // \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\"    -> tail = \"RJ\"\n            // \"Boavista ... - RJ\"   -> tail = \"RJ\"\n            if (tail.Length <= 3 && States.Contains(tail))\n                return (value.Substring(0, dashIndex), tail.ToUpperInvariant());\n\n            var parts = tail.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);\n            if (parts.Length == 1 && States.Contains(parts[0]))\n                return (value.Substring(0, dashIndex), parts[0].ToUpperInvariant());\n\n            dashIndex = value.LastIndexOf('-', dashIndex - 1);\n        }\n        return (value, null);\n    }\n}\n","filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs","time":{"start":1782088673159,"end":1782088673169}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Confirmed: 2019 has both \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\" (not GO). My normalizer stripped the state and merged them → \"Atletico\" with 112 pts (both Atlético-MG and Athletico-PR combined). The real 2019 champion is Flamengo (90 pts). \n\nI need to keep the state in the team identity. Let me refactor:\n\n1. TeamNameNormalizer: add `StateCode(raw)`, `BaseName(raw)`, `BaseKey(raw)`, `FullKey(raw)`.\n2. Service: index by FullKey. For bare-name queries, match on BaseKey (aggregating all states — acceptable for \"all Atletico matches\"). For standings, group by FullKey and display name includes state.\n\nLet me also consider: \"Atletico-MG\" display = \"Atletico-MG\"? Or \"Atletico\"? For standings, to distinguish, include state: \"Atletico-MG\". For general display of a uniquely-identified team, the bare name is nicer (\"Palmeiras\"). Let me make ResolveTeam smart: if baseKey maps to one fullKey, return baseName; else return baseName + \"-\" + state.\n\nLet me rewrite.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecc2fda4001OiyZ6SnUV504TG","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecc2ed8d001XKeUznszDMC5x4"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1782088673172,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"id":"prt_eecc2fce8001ZHM4lxavSGquuf","messageID":"msg_eecc2ed8d001XKeUznszDMC5x4","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","type":"text","text":"I need to keep the state in the team identity to avoid merging distinct clubs. Let me refactor the normalizer.","time":{"start":1782088662248,"end":1782088673170}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1782088673317,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"id":"prt_eecc32822001sJ1AveTOb5NgY4","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"0ea9b408aa1ee1df936814822291f4c79a40b27d","messageID":"msg_eecc2ed8d001XKeUznszDMC5x4","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":62736,"input":2799,"output":1151,"reasoning":248,"cache":{"write":0,"read":58538}},"cost":0.0208023}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1782088676873,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"id":"prt_eecc33603001hpAVLuk5ZL066u","messageID":"msg_eecc328a0001n6q46VotGB6G8x","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","snapshot":"0ea9b408aa1ee1df936814822291f4c79a40b27d","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782088730889,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_471eabc8aa05456599b83d98","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"// BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core - Query service.\n// The single entry point for all MCP tools. It indexes all loaded matches and\n// players by full team identity (base+state) so distinct same-base clubs\n// (Atletico-MG vs Atletico-PR) stay separate in standings, while bare-name\n// queries (\"all Atletico matches\") aggregate across states as users expect.\nusing BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core.Data;\nusing BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core.Models;\n\nnamespace BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core.Services;\n\npublic sealed class SoccerQueryService\n{\n    private readonly IReadOnlyList<Match> _matches;\n    private readonly IReadOnlyList<Player> _players;\n\n    // fullKey -> display (\"Atletico-MG\"), keyed by canonical identity.\n    private readonly Dictionary<string, string> _fullDisplay = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n    // fullKey -> matches involving that team.\n    private readonly Dictionary<string, List<Match>> _byFull = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n    // baseKey -> set of fullKeys (for resolving bare-name queries & derbies).\n    private readonly Dictionary<string, HashSet<string>> _baseToFulls = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n    // baseKey -> display base name (\"Atletico\").\n    private readonly Dictionary<string, string> _baseDisplay = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n\n    public SoccerQueryService(IReadOnlyList<Match> matches, IReadOnlyList<Player> players)\n    {\n        _matches = matches;\n        _players = players;\n\n        foreach (var m in matches)\n        {\n            IndexTeam(m.HomeTeam, m);\n            IndexTeam(m.AwayTeam, m);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<Match> AllMatches => _matches;\n    public IReadOnlyList<Player> AllPlayers => _players;\n    public IEnumerable<string> KnownTeams => _fullDisplay.Values;\n\n    private void IndexTeam(string rawName, Match m)\n    {\n        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(rawName)) return;\n        var full = TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(rawName);\n        if (full.Length == 0 || full == \"|\") return;\n\n        if (!_byFull.TryGetValue(full, out var list))\n        {\n            list = new List<Match>();\n            _byFull[full] = list;\n        }\n        list.Add(m);\n\n        var display = TeamNameNormalizer.DisplayName(rawName);\n        var baseName = TeamNameNormalizer.BaseName(rawName);\n        var baseKey = TeamNameNormalizer.BaseKey(rawName);\n\n        _fullDisplay.TryGetValue(full, out var existing);\n        if (existing is null || display.Length < existing.Length) _fullDisplay[full] = display;\n        if (baseKey.Length > 0)\n        {\n            if (!_baseToFulls.TryGetValue(baseKey, out var set)) { set = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.Ordinal); _baseToFulls[baseKey] = set; }\n            set.Add(full);\n            if (!_baseDisplay.TryGetValue(baseKey, out var b) || baseName.Length < b.Length) _baseDisplay[baseKey] = baseName;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Resolution helpers\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    /// <summary>\n    /// Resolves a user-supplied team name to a canonical display name.\n    /// If the name carries a state, the unique full identity is used. If the\n    /// bare name maps to exactly one club, that club is used. Otherwise the\n    /// bare display name is returned (queries will aggregate across states).\n    /// </summary>\n    public string ResolveTeam(string teamName)\n    {\n        var full = TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(teamName);\n        var state = TeamNameNormalizer.StateCode(teamName);\n        if (state.Length > 0 && _fullDisplay.TryGetValue(full, out var d)) return d;\n        var baseKey = TeamNameNormalizer.BaseKey(teamName);\n        if (baseKey.Length > 0 && _baseToFulls.TryGetValue(baseKey, out var fulls))\n        {\n            if (fulls.Count == 1) return _fullDisplay[fulls.First()];\n            return _baseDisplay.TryGetValue(baseKey, out var b) ? b : TeamNameNormalizer.BaseName(teamName);\n        }\n        return TeamNameNormalizer.DisplayName(teamName);\n    }\n\n    /// <summary>Returns the set of full team identities matching a (possibly bare) name.</summary>\n    private IEnumerable<string> ResolveFulls(string teamName)\n    {\n        var full = TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(teamName);\n        var state = TeamNameNormalizer.StateCode(teamName);\n        if (state.Length > 0)\n        {\n            if (_byFull.ContainsKey(full)) return new[] { full };\n            return Array.Empty<string>();\n        }\n        var baseKey = TeamNameNormalizer.BaseKey(teamName);\n        return _baseToFulls.TryGetValue(baseKey, out var set) ? set.ToArray() : Array.Empty<string>();\n    }\n\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Match queries\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<Match> FindMatchesByTeam(\n        string teamName,\n        Competition? competition = null, int? season = null,\n        DateTime? from = null, DateTime? to = null)\n    {\n        var matches = new List<Match>();\n        foreach (var full in ResolveFulls(teamName))\n        {\n            if (_byFull.TryGetValue(full, out var list))\n                matches.AddRange(list.Where(m => PassesFilters(m, competition, season, from, to)));\n        }\n        return matches.OrderBy(m => m.Date).ToList();\n    }\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<Match> FindMatchesBetweenTeams(\n        string teamA, string teamB,\n        Competition? competition = null, int? season = null)\n    {\n        var fullsA = ResolveFulls(teamA);\n        var fullsB = ResolveFulls(teamB);\n        var setA = new HashSet<string>(fullsA, StringComparer.Ordinal);\n        var setB = new HashSet<string>(fullsB, StringComparer.Ordinal);\n        return _matches.Where(m =>\n            {\n                var h = TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(m.HomeTeam);\n                var a = TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(m.AwayTeam);\n                return (setA.Contains(h) && setB.Contains(a)) ||\n                       (setA.Contains(a) && setB.Contains(h));\n            })\n            .Where(m => PassesFilters(m, competition, season))\n            .OrderBy(m => m.Date).ToList();\n    }\n\n    public Match? FindMostRecentMatch(string teamA, string teamB)\n        => FindMatchesBetweenTeams(teamA, teamB).MaxBy(m => m.Date);\n\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Team stats\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    public TeamStats GetTeamStats(\n        string teamName, Competition? competition = null, int? season = null)\n    {\n        var fulls = ResolveFulls(teamName).ToList();\n        var matches = FindMatchesByTeam(teamName, competition, season);\n        int w = 0, d = 0, l = 0, gf = 0, ga = 0;\n        int hw = 0, hd = 0, hl = 0, aw = 0, ad = 0, al = 0;\n        foreach (var m in matches)\n        {\n            bool isHome = fulls.Contains(TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(m.HomeTeam));\n            int forGoals = isHome ? m.HomeGoal : m.AwayGoal;\n            int against = isHome ? m.AwayGoal : m.HomeGoal;\n            gf += forGoals; ga += against;\n            if (forGoals > against) { w++; if (isHome) hw++; else aw++; }\n            else if (forGoals == against) { d++; if (isHome) hd++; else ad++; }\n            else { l++; if (isHome) hl++; else al++; }\n        }\n        return new TeamStats\n        {\n            Team = ResolveTeam(teamName),\n            Matches = matches.Count,\n            Wins = w, Draws = d, Losses = l,\n            GoalsFor = gf, GoalsAgainst = ga,\n            HomeMatches = hw + hd + hl, HomeWins = hw, HomeDraws = hd, HomeLosses = hl,\n            AwayMatches = aw + ad + al, AwayWins = aw, AwayDraws = ad, AwayLosses = al,\n            Points = w * 3 + d\n        };\n    }\n\n    public HeadToHead GetHeadToHead(string teamA, string teamB)\n    {\n        var fullsA = ResolveFulls(teamA).ToHashSet(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n        var fullsB = ResolveFulls(teamB).ToHashSet(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n        var matches = FindMatchesBetweenTeams(teamA, teamB);\n        int aw = 0, bw = 0, dr = 0;\n        foreach (var m in matches)\n        {\n            var hFull = TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(m.HomeTeam);\n            var aFull = TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(m.AwayTeam);\n            bool aHome = fullsA.Contains(hFull);\n            int aGoals = aHome ? m.HomeGoal : m.AwayGoal;\n            int bGoals = aHome ? m.AwayGoal : m.HomeGoal;\n            if (aGoals > bGoals) aw++;\n            else if (aGoals < bGoals) bw++;\n            else dr++;\n        }\n        return new HeadToHead\n        {\n            TeamA = ResolveTeam(teamA), TeamB = ResolveTeam(teamB),\n            TeamAWins = aw, TeamBWins = bw, Draws = dr,\n            Matches = matches.Count, MatchesList = matches\n        };\n    }\n\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Standings\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    public IEnumerable<int> AvailableSeasons(Competition? competition = null) =>\n        _matches.Where(m => competition == null || m.Competition == competition)\n                .Select(m => m.Season).Distinct().OrderBy(s => s);\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<StandingsRow> GetStandings(int season, Competition competition)\n    {\n        var seasonMatches = _matches.Where(m => m.Season == season && m.Competition == competition).ToList();\n        var table = new Dictionary<string, StandingsAcc>(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n        foreach (var m in seasonMatches)\n        {\n            Acc(table, m.HomeTeam, m.HomeGoal, m.AwayGoal);\n            Acc(table, m.AwayTeam, m.AwayGoal, m.HomeGoal);\n        }\n        var rows = table.Select(kv =>\n        {\n            var a = kv.Value;\n            var display = _fullDisplay.TryGetValue(kv.Key, out var d) ? d\n                : TeamNameNormalizer.DisplayName(kv.Key);\n            return new StandingsRow\n            {\n                Team = display,\n                Played = a.Played, Wins = a.Wins, Draws = a.Draws, Losses = a.Losses,\n                GoalsFor = a.GoalsFor, GoalsAgainst = a.GoalsAgainst,\n                Points = a.Wins * 3 + a.Draws\n            };\n        })\n        .OrderByDescending(r => r.Points)\n        .ThenByDescending(r => r.GoalDifference)\n        .ThenByDescending(r => r.GoalsFor)\n        .ThenBy(r => r.Team)\n        .Select((r, i) => r with { Position = i + 1 })\n        .ToList();\n\n        if (rows.Count > 0) rows[0] = rows[0] with { Champion = true };\n        return rows;\n    }\n\n    private void Acc(Dictionary<string, StandingsAcc> table, string team, int gf, int ga)\n    {\n        var full = TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(team);\n        if (full.Length == 0 || full == \"|\") return;\n        if (!table.TryGetValue(full, out var acc)) { acc = new StandingsAcc(); table[full] = acc; }\n        acc.Played++;\n        acc.GoalsFor += gf; acc.GoalsAgainst += ga;\n        if (gf > ga) acc.Wins++; else if (gf == ga) acc.Draws++; else acc.Losses++;\n    }\n\n    private sealed class StandingsAcc\n    {\n        public int Played, Wins, Draws, Losses, GoalsFor, GoalsAgainst;\n    }\n\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Statistics\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    public double AverageGoalsPerMatch(Competition? competition = null, int? season = null)\n    {\n        var subset = _matches.Where(m => PassesFilters(m, competition, season)).ToList();\n        if (subset.Count == 0) return 0;\n        return (double)subset.Sum(m => m.HomeGoal + m.AwayGoal) / subset.Count;\n    }\n\n    public (double HomeWinRate, double DrawRate, double AwayWinRate) WinRateBreakdown(\n        Competition? competition = null, int? season = null)\n    {\n        var subset = _matches.Where(m => PassesFilters(m, competition, season)).ToList();\n        if (subset.Count == 0) return (0, 0, 0);\n        int hw = subset.Count(m => m.HomeGoal > m.AwayGoal);\n        int dr = subset.Count(m => m.HomeGoal == m.AwayGoal);\n        int aw = subset.Count(m => m.HomeGoal < m.AwayGoal);\n        double n = subset.Count;\n        return (hw / n, dr / n, aw / n);\n    }\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<Match> BiggestWins(\n        Competition? competition = null, int? season = null, int top = 10)\n        => _matches.Where(m => PassesFilters(m, competition, season))\n                   .OrderByDescending(m => m.GoalDifference)\n                   .ThenByDescending(m => m.HomeGoal + m.AwayGoal)\n                   .Take(top).ToList();\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<TeamStats> BestAwayRecords(\n        Competition? competition = null, int? season = null, int minMatches = 10)\n        => _fullDisplay.Keys\n            .Select(k => GetTeamStats(_fullDisplay[k], competition, season))\n            .Where(s => s.AwayMatches >= minMatches)\n            .OrderByDescending(s => s.AwayWinRate).ThenByDescending(s => s.AwayWins).ToList();\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<TeamStats> BestHomeRecords(\n        Competition? competition = null, int? season = null, int minMatches = 10)\n        => _fullDisplay.Keys\n            .Select(k => GetTeamStats(_fullDisplay[k], competition, season))\n            .Where(s => s.HomeMatches >= minMatches)\n            .OrderByDescending(s => s.HomeWinRate).ThenByDescending(s => s.HomeWins).ToList();\n\n    public TeamStats? TopScoringTeam(\n        Competition? competition = null, int? season = null)\n        => _fullDisplay.Keys\n            .Select(k => GetTeamStats(_fullDisplay[k], competition, season))\n            .OrderByDescending(s => s.GoalsFor).FirstOrDefault();\n\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Players\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<Player> FindPlayers(\n        string? name = null, string? nationality = null, string? club = null,\n        string? position = null, int? minOverall = null, int? maxOverall = null, int? top = null)\n    {\n        var q = _players.AsEnumerable();\n        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(name))\n        {\n            var nm = name.Trim();\n            q = q.Where(p => p.Name.Contains(nm, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n        }\n        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(nationality))\n            q = q.Where(p => p.Nationality.Equals(nationality, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(club))\n        {\n            var c = club.Trim();\n            q = q.Where(p => p.Club.Contains(c, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n        }\n        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(position))\n            q = q.Where(p => p.Position.Equals(position, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase));\n        if (minOverall.HasValue) q = q.Where(p => p.Overall >= minOverall.Value);\n        if (maxOverall.HasValue) q = q.Where(p => p.Overall <= maxOverall.Value);\n        q = q.OrderByDescending(p => p.Overall);\n        if (top.HasValue) q = q.Take(top.Value);\n        return q.ToList();\n    }\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<Player> TopBrazilianPlayers(int top = 10)\n        => _players.Where(p => p.IsBrazilian)\n                   .OrderByDescending(p => p.Overall).Take(top).ToList();\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<Player> PlayersAtClub(string club, int? top = null)\n        => FindPlayers(club: club, top: top);\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<(string Club, int Count, double AvgRating)> BrazilianPlayersAtBrazilianClubs()\n    {\n        var clubFulls = new HashSet<string>(_fullDisplay.Keys, StringComparer.Ordinal);\n        return _players\n            .Where(p => p.IsBrazilian && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.Club))\n            .GroupBy(p => p.Club)\n            .Where(g => clubFulls.Contains(TeamNameNormalizer.FullKey(g.Key)))\n            .Select(g => (Club: g.Key, Count: g.Count(), AvgRating: g.Average(p => p.Overall)))\n            .OrderByDescending(t => t.Count).ToList();\n    }\n\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // Derbies\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    private static readonly (string A, string B)[] DerbyRivals =\n    {\n        (\"Flamengo\",\"Fluminense\"), (\"Flamengo\",\"Vasco\"), (\"Vasco\",\"Flamengo\"),\n        (\"Corinthians\",\"Palmeiras\"), (\"Corinthians\",\"São Paulo\"), (\"Palmeiras\",\"São Paulo\"),\n        (\"Santos\",\"São Paulo\"), (\"Santos\",\"Corinthians\"),\n        (\"Grêmio\",\"Internacional\"), (\"Internacional\",\"Grêmio\"),\n        (\"Atlético-MG\",\"Cruzeiro\"), (\"Cruzeiro\",\"Atlético Mineiro\"),\n        (\"Bahia\",\"Vitória\"), (\"Fortaleza\",\"Ceará\"),\n        (\"Sport\",\"Náutico\"), (\"Coritiba\",\"Athletico-PR\"),\n    };\n\n    public IReadOnlyList<Match> FindDerbies(int? season = null, Competition? competition = null)\n    {\n        var rivalBases = DerbyRivals\n            .Select(p => (A: TeamNameNormalizer.BaseKey(p.A), B: TeamNameNormalizer.BaseKey(p.B)))\n            .Where(p => p.A.Length > 0 && p.B.Length > 0)\n            .ToHashSet();\n\n        bool IsDerby(Match m)\n        {\n            var h = TeamNameNormalizer.BaseKey(m.HomeTeam);\n            var a = TeamNameNormalizer.BaseKey(m.AwayTeam);\n            return rivalBases.Contains((h, a));\n        }\n\n        return _matches.Where(m => PassesFilters(m, competition, season) && IsDerby(m))\n                       .OrderBy(m => m.Date).ToList();\n    }\n\n    // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    private static bool PassesFilters(Match m, Competition? competition, int? season = null,\n        DateTime? from = null, DateTime? to = null)\n    {\n        if (competition.HasValue && m.Competition != competition.Value) return false;\n        if (season.HasValue && m.Season != season.Value) return false;\n        if (from.HasValue && m.Date < from.Value) return false;\n        if (to.HasValue && m.Date > to.Value) return false;\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n","filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs","time":{"start":1782088730871,"end":1782088730887}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_eecc3371f001q7EyWGfxiPjfXN","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecc328a0001n6q46VotGB6G8x"}}
