splay[full] = bare;\n+            else _fullDisplay[full] = TeamNameNormalizer.DisplayName(_fullDisplay[full]);\n+        }\n+    }\n }\n \n public IReadOnlyList<Match> AllMatches => _matches;\n public IReadOnlyList<Player> AllPlayers => _players;\n","additions":13,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs","time":{"start":1782088757137,"end":1782088757154}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now Flamengo is correctly the 2019 champion with 90 pts. The Atletico-PR and Atletico-MG are now distinct. \n\nThe state suffix appears in display names now (Flamengo-RJ, Palmeiras-SP). That's correct/expected per the spec which says \"With state suffix\". For a cleaner display, the bare name is nicer for uniquely-identified teams, but since most Brazilian team base names are unique within the dataset, I could omit the state when unambiguous. But \"Atletico\" base is ambiguous (Atletico-PR, Atletico-MG) so we keep state for those. The current DisplayName always includes state when present. That's fine and matches the source data. The spec example shows \"Flamengo\" without state in formatted output though: \"1. Flamengo - 90 pts (28W, 6D, 4L) - Champion\". So for nicer output, drop the state when unambiguous.\n\nLet me improve ResolveTeam and the standings display: when the baseKey maps to exactly one fullKey, display the bare base name; otherwise show with state. The _fullDisplay map currently stores DisplayName (with state). Let me adjust: store the \"smart\" display — bare name when unambiguous, else with state.\n\nBut the indexing happens before all teams are seen, so I can't decide ambiguity at index time easily. Let me do a post-pass: after loading all matches, iterate _baseToFulls and for each full, decide display: if its baseKey has only one full → bare base; else base-state.\n\nLet me add a `FinalizeDisplay` step in the constructor after the loop.\n\nLet me update."