{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782088841353,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_37a2472c32f04b54b234e9cb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs","newString":"    public IReadOnlyList<StandingsRow> GetStandings(int season, Competition competition)\n    {\n        var seasonMatches = _matches.Where(m => m.Season == season && m.Competition == competition).ToList();\n        var table = new Dictionary<string, StandingsAcc>(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n        foreach (var m in seasonMatches)\n        {\n            Acc(table, m.HomeTeam, m.HomeGoal, m.AwayGoal);\n            Acc(table, m.AwayTeam, m.AwayGoal, m.HomeGoal);\n        }\n\n马鞍_0\n    }","oldString":"    public IReadOnlyList<StandingsRow> GetStandings(int season, Competition competition)\n    {\n        var seasonMatches = _matches.Where(m => m.Season == season && m.Competition == competition).ToList();\n        var table = new Dictionary<string, StandingsAcc>(StringComparer.Ordinal);\n        foreach (var m in seasonMatches)\n        {\n            Acc(table, m.HomeTeam, m.HomeGoal, m.AwayGoal);\n            Acc(table, m.AwayTeam, m.AwayGoal, m.HomeGoal);\n        }\n        var rows = table.Select(kv =>\n        {\n            var a = kv.Value;\n            var display = _fullDisplay.TryGetValue(kv.Key, out var d) ? d\n                : TeamNameNormalizer.DisplayName(kv.Key);\n            return new StandingsRow\n            {\n                Team = display,\n                Played = a.Played, Wins = a.Wins, Draws = a.Draws, Losses = a.Losses,\n                GoalsFor = a.GoalsFor, GoalsAgainst = a.GoalsAgainst,\n                Points = a.Wins * 3 + a.Draws\n            };\n        })\n        .OrderByDescending(r => r.Points)\n        .ThenByDescending(r => r.GoalDifference)\n        .ThenByDescending(r => r.GoalsFor)\n        .ThenBy(r => r.Team)\n        .Select((r, i) => r with { Position = i + 1 })\n        .ToList();\n\n        if (rows.Count > 0) rows[0] = rows[0] with { Champion = true };\n        return rows;\n    }"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs\n@@ -230,30 +230,10 @@\n         {\n             Acc(table, m.HomeTeam, m.HomeGoal, m.AwayGoal);\n             Acc(table, m.AwayTeam, m.AwayGoal, m.HomeGoal);\n         }\n-        var rows = table.Select(kv =>\n-        {\n-            var a = kv.Value;\n-            var display = _fullDisplay.TryGetValue(kv.Key, out var d) ? d\n-                : TeamNameNormalizer.DisplayName(kv.Key);\n-            return new StandingsRow\n-            {\n-                Team = display,\n-                Played = a.Played, Wins = a.Wins, Draws = a.Draws, Losses = a.Losses,\n-                GoalsFor = a.GoalsFor, GoalsAgainst = a.GoalsAgainst,\n-                Points = a.Wins * 3 + a.Draws\n-            };\n-        })\n-        .OrderByDescending(r => r.Points)\n-        .ThenByDescending(r => r.GoalDifference)\n-        .ThenByDescending(r => r.GoalsFor)\n-        .ThenBy(r => r.Team)\n-        .Select((r, i) => r with { Position = i + 1 })\n-        .ToList();\n \n-        if (rows.Count > 0) rows[0] = rows[0] with { Champion = true };\n-        return rows;\n+马鞍_0\n     }\n \n     private void Acc(Dictionary<string, StandingsAcc> table, string team, int gf, int ga)\n     {\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-1zdmpvud/retort-f437e3d99e40/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs\n@@ -230,30 +230,10 @@\n         {\n             Acc(table, m.HomeTeam, m.HomeGoal, m.AwayGoal);\n             Acc(table, m.AwayTeam, m.AwayGoal, m.HomeGoal);\n         }\n-        var rows = table.Select(kv =>\n-        {\n-            var a = kv.Value;\n-            var display = _fullDisplay.TryGetValue(kv.Key, out var d) ? d\n-                : TeamNameNormalizer.DisplayName(kv.Key);\n-            return new StandingsRow\n-            {\n-                Team = display,\n-                Played = a.Played, Wins = a.Wins, Draws = a.Draws, Losses = a.Losses,\n-                GoalsFor = a.GoalsFor, GoalsAgainst = a.GoalsAgainst,\n-                Points = a.Wins * 3 + a.Draws\n-            };\n-        })\n-        .OrderByDescending(r => r.Points)\n-        .ThenByDescending(r => r.GoalDifference)\n-        .ThenByDescending(r => r.GoalsFor)\n-        .ThenBy(r => r.Team)\n-        .Select((r, i) => r with { Position = i + 1 })\n-        .ToList();\n \n-        if (rows.Count > 0) rows[0] = rows[0] with { Champion = true };\n-        return rows;\n+马鞍_0\n     }\n \n     private void Acc(Dictionary<string, StandingsAcc> table, string team, int gf, int ga)\n     {\n","additions":1,"deletions":21},"truncated":false},"title":"src/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Core/Services/SoccerQueryService.cs","time":{"start":1782088841350,"end":1782088841352}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So Flamengo appears as \"Flamengo\" (no state, in Libertadores/Brazilian_Cup maybe), \"Flamengo-RJ\" (Brasileirao), \"Flamengo - RJ\" (Copa do Brasil with spaced dash), and even \"Flamengo - PI\"/\"Flamengo do Piauí - PI\" (a different minor club from Piauí state!). \n\nSo base key \"flamengo\" maps to multiple fulls: \"flamengo|rj\", \"flamengo|\" (from Libertadores where no state), and \"flamengo|pi\" (Flamengo do Piauí? Wait \"Flamengo do Piauí - PI\" → base name strips state → \"Flamengo do Piauí\" → base key \"flamengo do piaui\", different base. And \"Flamengo - PI\" → base \"Flamengo\" + state PI → \"flamengo|pi\". So that's a DIFFERENT club — Flamengo-PI (Flamengo do Piauí's short name?). Hmm.\n\nSo actually base \"flamengo\" maps to: \"flamengo|rj\" (the real Flamengo-RJ), \"flamengo|\" (Libertadores, no state — same club as Flamengo-RJ really, just missing state in that file), and \"flamengo|pi\" (a different minor club). So my logic sees count=3 and keeps state suffix → \"Flamengo-RJ\".\n\nThe real fix: the stateless \"Flamengo\" entries in Libertadores ARE the same Flamengo-RJ club. The \"Flamengo-PI\" is genuinely different. So base→fulls = {rj, \"\", pi}. Three entries; two of them (rj and \"\") are the same club; pi is different.\n\nThis is the crux of the data-quality problem: the same club appears with and without state across files. We want to merge \"flamengo|rj\" and \"flamengo|\" (stateless) into one club when there's no other state for that base. But \"flamengo|pi\" should stay separate.\n\nA cleaner approach: when a base name appears both with state X and without state (empty), and there's no OTHER conflicting state, merge the stateless entries into the state-X club. If there are multiple states and also stateless, the stateless ones are ambiguous — could be any. But practically, the stateless ones usually refer to the most prominent club.\n\nPragmatic rule for finalization:\n- For each base, look at the set of non-empty states. \n  - If there's exactly ONE non-empty state, then all stateless fulls belong to that state's club. Merge them: treat \"flamengo|\" as alias of \"flamengo|rj\".\n  - If there are multiple non-empty states (e.g. Atletico has PR and MG, plus maybe stateless), the stateless ones are ambiguous — leave them as a separate \"Atletico\" bucket (bare). \n\nThis way:\n- Flamengo: states {RJ, PI} (two non-empty). Wait, Flamengo-PI exists. So non-empty states = {rj, pi}. Two distinct. Then stateless \"Flamengo\" (Libertadores) is ambiguous between RJ and PI. Hmm, but RJ is the famous one; PI is a tiny club. Practically the Libertadores \"Flamengo\" is the RJ one (Flamengo-PI never plays Libertadores). But our rule can't know.\n\nThis is getting complicated. Let me simplify for the benchmark: \n\nGoal: Make the 2019 Brasileirão standings show \"Flamengo\" (not \"Flamengo-RJ\") to match the spec example, AND keep Atletico-MG/PR distinct, AND not break cross-file queries.\n\nSimplest approach that satisfies the spec example: For DISPLAY, drop the state suffix always (show bare base name). For STANDINGS grouping, keep the full key (so Atletico-MG and Atletico-PR remain distinct rows, but both display as \"Atletico\" — which is confusing in a standings table!). \n\nHmm. The spec example shows \"1. Flamengo - 90 pts ... - Champion\" with no state. And \"5. Atletico-PR\" wasn't in spec example. The spec doesn't have Atletico ambiguity in its example.\n\nFor a clean demo, let me:\n- Display: bare base name when the base maps to exactly ONE state (ignoring stateless entries as aliases of the single state). When multiple states, show base-state. When only stateless (no states at all for that base), show bare.\n- Group standings by full key (so distinct states are distinct rows).\n- For Flamengo: states = {rj, pi}. Multiple states → display with state → \"Flamengo-RJ\" and \"Flamengo-PI\". The Libertadores stateless \"Flamengo\" would be its own row \"Flamengo\" in Libertadores standings (different competition, different season — not in 2019 Brasileirão). For 2019 Brasileirão, only \"Flamengo-RJ\" appears → in that season/competition, the base \"flamengo\" maps to only one state (rj) → display \"Flamengo\". \n\nBut my display finalization is global (across all competitions), not per-season. So Flamengo globally has states {rj, pi, \"\"} → ambiguous → \"Flamengo-RJ\".\n\nBetter: make display resolution per-call. For standings, when building rows, for each full key, decide display based on the OTHER fulls in the SAME season/competition table. If in the 2019 Brasileirão table there's only one \"flamengo*\" full, display \"Flamengo\"; if there are two Atletico*, display \"Atletico-PR\"/\"Atletico-MG\".\n\nActually that's clean and local. Let me change the standings display logic: within GetStandings, after building the table (set of full keys), for each full, compute display: if its baseKey is unique among the table's fulls → bare base; else → base-state.\n\nSimilarly for ResolveTeam (single team): if the bare name resolves to one full globally → bare; else base-state. That's what I had but it considers ALL fulls globally including the PI club. Hmm.\n\nFor the team-stats display (single team), showing \"Flamengo-RJ\" is acceptable actually. The spec example for team stats: \"Corinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão):\" — no state. So bare preferred. \n\nLet me make ResolveTeam use bare when the base maps to a single full INCLUDING treating stateless as alias of the single non-empty state. That is: \n- non-empty states for the base = set of states (excluding \"\")\n- if non-empty states count == 1: the canonical club is that state; bare name is fine. (Flamengo: non-empty = {rj, pi} → count 2 → ambiguous → show state.)\n  - But wait, Flamengo-PI is a tiny club; in practice queries about \"Flamengo\" mean RJ. But we can't know. For the benchmark, showing \"Flamengo-RJ\" for team queries is acceptable.\n- For 2019 Brasileirão STANDINGS though, only Flamengo-RJ appears (no Flamengo-PI in 2019 Serie A). So per-table display → bare \"Flamengo\". \n\nSo the per-table (per-standings) display logic gives the spec's expected \"1. Flamengo - 90 pts\". Let me implement that.\n\nLet me change GetStandings to compute display per-table:\n- Collect fulls in table. Group by baseKey. For each full, if its baseKey appears once in the table → display bare base; else → base-state (using the global _fullDisplay which has state).\n\nImplementation: after building `table` dict (full→acc), before constructing rows, compute baseKey for each full in table, count occurrences. Then display = (count==1 ? baseDisplay[baseKey] : _fullDisplay[full]).\n\nLet me also update ResolveTeam to handle the empty-state aliasing for single-team display. Actually for single team, the user usually queries \"Flamengo\" meaning the famous one. Let me keep ResolveTeam as: if base maps to 1 full → bare; if multiple → show with state (Flamengo-RJ). That's acceptable. But \"Flamengo\" base maps to {rj, pi, \"\"} = 3 → show with state. The stateless \"Flamengo\" Libertadores entries — for a team stats query \"Flamengo\", ResolveFulls returns all 3 → aggregates Flamengo-RJ + Flamengo(stateless=Libertadores) + Flamengo-PI matches. That includes the PI club's matches (few) — slightly wrong but minor.\n\nHmm. Actually the PI club \"Flamengo - PI\" / \"Flamengo do Piauí\" is a separate minor club. \"FindMatchesByTeam('Flamengo')\" would include their matches too. That's a known limitation; the user can disambiguate with \"Flamengo-RJ\".\n\nFor the benchmark, let me accept this. The key fix is the 2019 standings display showing \"Flamengo\" not \"Flamengo-RJ\". Let me implement per-table display in GetStandings.\n\nLet me also reconsider: should I even keep the global FinalizeDisplay? It sets _fullDisplay to bare when global base→1 full. That helps teams like Palmeiras (only Palmeiras-SP, no other state, no stateless? Actually Palmeiras might appear stateless in Libertadores too). Let me check Palmeiras. Actually it doesn't matter much. Let me keep the global finalize but also add per-table display in standings.\n\nLet me just edit GetStandings.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecc58946001A0xOtoC5ELw7vU","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecc51b0c0018koeAbgnicq3ip"}}
