{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782088921252,"sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-958feb6e5abe4bbf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -E 'M:LightBDD.Framework.IBddRunner\\.|M:LightBDD.Framework.Extensibility.BddRunnerExtensions\\.' /Users/maui/.nuget/packages/lightbdd.framework/3.12.0/lib/net6.0/LightBDD.Framework.xml | head -20; echo \"---IScenarioBuilder---\"; grep -E 'M:LightBDD.Framework.Scenarios.IScenarioBuilder\\.|T:LightBDD.Framework.Scenarios.IScenarioBuilder|M:LightBDD.Framework.Scenarios.ScenarioBuilderExtensions|IScenarioBuilder`1' /Users/maui/.nuget/packages/lightbdd.framework/3.12.0/lib/net6.0/LightBDD.Framework.xml | head -20","description":"Inspect IBddRunner and scenario builder"},"output":"        <member name=\"M:LightBDD.Framework.Extensibility.BddRunnerExtensions.GetBddRunner(LightBDD.Core.Extensibility.IFeatureRunner,System.Object)\">\r\n---IScenarioBuilder---\n        <member name=\"T:LightBDD.Framework.Scenarios.IScenarioBuilder`1\">\r\n        <member name=\"M:LightBDD.Framework.Scenarios.IScenarioBuilder`1.Integrate\">\r\n","metadata":{"output":"        <member name=\"M:LightBDD.Framework.Extensibility.BddRunnerExtensions.GetBddRunner(LightBDD.Core.Extensibility.IFeatureRunner,System.Object)\">\r\n---IScenarioBuilder---\n        <member name=\"T:LightBDD.Framework.Scenarios.IScenarioBuilder`1\">\r\n        <member name=\"M:LightBDD.Framework.Scenarios.IScenarioBuilder`1.Integrate\">\r\n","exit":0,"description":"Inspect IBddRunner and scenario builder","truncated":false},"title":"Inspect IBddRunner and scenario builder","time":{"start":1782088921249,"end":1782088921250}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"`RunScenario(IBddRunner, params Action[])`. But that doesn't give step names — the step names come from the method names of the Action delegates. So `RunScenario(_ => Given_data_loaded(), _ => When_I_search(...), _ => Then_...)` would name steps from the lambda body? Actually LightBDD's BasicExtensions.RunScenario uses the delegate method names as step names. But lambdas produce compiler-generated names. The recommended pattern is to pass method group delegates:\n\n```csharp\nRunner.RunScenario(\n    Given_the_match_data_is_loaded,\n    When_I_search_for_matches_between_Flamengo_and_Fluminense,\n    Then_I_should_receive_a_list_of_matches);\n```\n\nwhere each is a method `void Given_the_match_data_is_loaded()`. The step names derive from method names. That's the clean BDD style.\n\nBut I need to pass parameters. Method groups with parameters: `When_I_search_for_matches_between_Flamengo_and_Fluminense` is a parameterless method that calls the actual search with hardcoded args. That's verbose. Alternatively use the Compact API with explicit step text and lambdas via `AddStep`:\n\n```csharp\nRunner\n    .AddStep(\"Given the match data is loaded\", _ => { /* setup */ })\n    .AddStep(\"When I search for matches between \\\"Flamengo\\\" and \\\"Fluminense\\\"\", _ => { result = Query.FindMatchesBetweenTeams(\"Flamengo\",\"Fluminense\"); })\n    .AddStep(\"Then I should receive a list of matches with date, scores and competition\", _ => Assert.NotEmpty(result))\n    .Run();\n```\n\nWait, `AddStep` signature is `AddStep<T>(IScenarioBuilder<T>, string, Action<T>)`. The `Runner` is `IBddRunner`. To get `IScenarioBuilder<T>` we call `Runner.NewScenario()`? Let me check. Actually `IBddRunner` has methods. The CompactExtensions.AddStep takes IScenarioBuilder<T>. The `Runner` (IBddRunner) probably exposes a `NewScenario()` returning IScenarioBuilder<NoContext>. Let me check.\n\nActually the basic pattern with `Runner.RunScenario(...)` is simpler. But for parameterized steps, I'll define helper methods. Actually let me use the Extended/Compact scenario builder. Let me check IBddRunner members.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecc6e905001cFFbfT7FFcVTYK","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecc6c7780013SCwvlPcxolgqN"}}
