 first line: \",ID,Name,...\". ParseLine splits on commas → first field is \"\" (empty string, trimmed). So headers[0]=\"\". Then _map[\"\"] = fields[0]. And _map[\"ID\"]=fields[1], etc. So Get(\"Club\") works correctly because the header \"Club\" maps to the right field. Good — the loader is fine.\n\nBut my awk used $9 which is wrong column. Let me check club via $10.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecca0327001sGaVkm6nsb3S7j","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecc9eb390010S9kQSpnKig1pz"}}
