 to use Cruzeiro and ST. \n\nNow let me fix all three tests:\n1. Derby test: expand IsDerby to recognize \"Atletico Mineiro\" base key. Add (cruzeiro, atletico mineiro) pair.\n2. Available seasons: change to 2019 and 2022.\n3. Player club test: use Cruzeiro instead of Sao Paulo.\n\nLet me also double check the derby service returned \"Cruzeiro vs Atletico Mineiro\" — that's from the historical file (2003-2019) which uses \"Atlético Mineiro\"? Actually the historical file uses \"Equipe_mandante\" = \"Cruzeiro\" and \"Atlético-MG\"? Let me check. The error said \"Cruzeiro vs Atletico Mineiro\" — so one team is \"Atletico Mineiro\" (full name without dash). That's from BR-Football-Dataset probably (which uses bare names like \"Cruzeiro\", \"Atletico Mineiro\"). The service's DerbyRivals has (\"Cruzeiro\",\"Atlético Mineiro\") → BaseKey \"cruzeiro\" and \"atletico mineiro\". And (\"Atlético-MG\",\"Cruzeiro\") → \"atletico\" and \"cruzeiro\". So the service detects Cruzeiro vs Atletico Mineiro via the second pair. Good. The test's IsDerby just needs to include both base key forms.\n\nActually, simpler: in the test, recognize a match as a derby if EITHER (a) it's in the test's known rival set OR (b) the service itself would classify it. But that's circular. Let me just expand the test's set to include \"atletico mineiro\". Let me update IsDerby to use base keys of: \"Atletico Mineiro\" and \"Cruzeiro\".\n\nLet me fix the three tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecca5266001dzGytf4zTfAHm4","sessionID":"ses_11343aad7ffeUJRsKWvvH5xMok","messageID":"msg_eecca392e001rLn33ZjaBFyTiK"}}
